cosider a number n. the ith digit n is called either maxima or minima if the digits at i-1 and i+1 are either greater than or less than
the digit i repspectively. The slope of n is defined as the no of maxima and minima present in n. If there is no digit at i-1 or i+2 for diit 
at i of the number n then do not consider digit at i for maxima or minima . Your task id to find and print the sum of the slooes of the number
with in the range a and b both incclusive. sample input a=1201 b= 1210
Code:
import java.util.*;
public class Main{
    static int slope(int n){
        String s=String.valueOf(n);
        int count=0;
        for(int i=1;i<s.length()-1;i++){
            int prev= s.charAt(i-1)-'0';
            int next= s.charAt(i+1)-'0';
            int curr= s.charAt(i)-'0';
            if(curr>prev && curr> next || curr<prev && curr < next){
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
        
    }
    public static void main(String[] args){
        Scanner sc= new Scanner(System.in);
        int a=sc.nextInt();
        int b=sc.nextInt();
        int sum=0;
        for(int n=a;n<=b;n++){
            sum+=slope(n);
        }
        System.out.println(sum);
    }
}
